1. Arithmetic Operators
These perform mathematical operations.
+	Addition	5 + 3	8
-	Subtraction	5 - 3	2
*	Multiplication	5 * 3	15
/	Division	5 / 2	2.5
//	Floor Division	5 // 2	2
%	Modulus (Remainder)	5 % 2	1
**	Exponent (Power)	5 ** 2	25

2.Comparitors
==
!=
<
>
>=
<=

3.Assigning opertaors
=	  x = 5 	Assign value
+=	x += 2	x = x + 2
-=	x -= 2	x = x - 2
*=	x *= 2	x = x * 2
/=	x /= 2	x = x / 2
%=	x %= 2	x = x % 2

4. Logical Operators
Used to combine conditions.
Operator ---->	Meaning
and	-----> True if both conditions are true
or	-----> True if at least one condition is true
not	-----> Reverses the result

5. Identity Operators
Check whether two variables refer to the same object.
Operator	----> Meaning
is ------>	Same object
is not	------> Different objects

6. Membership Operators
Check whether a value exists in a sequence.
Operator	----> Meaning
in	---> Value exists
not in	----> Value does not exist

7. Bitwise Operators (Advanced)
These work on the binary representation of integers.
Operator ---->	Meaning
&	---> AND
`	----> `
^	----> XOR
~	----> NOT
<<	----> Left shift
>>	----> Right shift
